WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.798 --> 00:00:01.631
(crowd cheering)

00:00:01.631 --> 00:00:02.850
- All right, y'all, let's close things out

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.950
with something I hope will
add some joy to your day.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.243
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.243 --> 00:00:08.237
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.237 --> 00:00:09.187
(audience cheering)

00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:10.648
There's something totally rewarding

00:00:10.648 --> 00:00:12.720
in lending help when
someone needs it most.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.520
An Ontario woman knows that all too well.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.260
After meeting a homeless man

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.630
in her neighborhood earlier
this year, she decided

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.490
to offer him work on her farm

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.810
but she didn't stop there.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.310
Now, not only does he have a roof

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.143
over his head,

00:00:24.143 --> 00:00:26.430
they both say their lives
are changed forever.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.160
We have them on the line
right now watching on Citytv.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.034
Everybody, give a big hello
to Danielle and Brian.

00:00:32.034 --> 00:00:33.420
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.270
What's up, y'all?

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.120
Oh my God, I wanna be where
you are, I love animals.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.200
So Danielle, as soon

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.120
as you learned Brian's
story, you took action.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.920
Can you tell everybody how you did that?

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.040
- Yes, so for weeks, I
had seen Brian sitting

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.580
outside our local drugstore,
collecting change.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.260
And I decided one day

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.860
that I needed to stop and
talk to him, and I did.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.590
And once I learned his story, I knew

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.860
that I needed to offer
him a job on my farm.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.480
So that, I did.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.970
And then I decided that, you know what?

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:10.953
He needed a haircut and we went
and took him for a haircut.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.060
Since then, Brian's just
really, really changed

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.250
and grown as a person.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.770
- Man, Brian, I mean,
that had to mean the world

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.232
to you that somebody took
the time not only to stop

00:01:22.232 --> 00:01:25.860
and talk to you, have
an actual conversation

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.320
but then offer you a
job, what was that like?

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.590
- It was amazing.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.280
It was wonderful and
I couldn't believe it.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.280
She helped me out greatly

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.070
and it was very nice
to have someone to stop

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.500
and actually, talk to me

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.470
and to see what I'd like about life.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.510
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:49.470
Well, Danielle,

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.050
Brian's also found
housing, correct, right?

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.400
- Yes, so that's right.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:57.660
One night, it was going to be
minus 20 degrees where we live

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.570
and I just couldn't bring
myself to drop him off

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.630
at his uninsulated shed
where he was living.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.830
So I did a post

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:09.000
on Facebook, asking our
community if they'd be willing

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.000
to donate $5 to help Brian
get a room for the night.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.880
And our community was
absolutely incredible

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.060
and came up with enough
money, not only for one night,

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.170
but for nine nights in a hotel room.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.720
And then I started a GoFundMe,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.360
which has now reached $11,000

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.960
and Brian now has a room in a house.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.230
- Oh, that's incredible.
(audience applauding)

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.063
That's incredible.

00:02:38.063 --> 00:02:38.896
'Cause, you know what?

00:02:38.896 --> 00:02:39.780
People wanna help, Danielle,

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.190
and they don't know how, always.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.780
And Brian, way to go, man.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.970
Congratulations on turning life around.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.590
Thank you so much, Brian.
(audience applauding)

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.030
Thank you, Danielle.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.310
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.725
- [Brian] I appreciate all the help.

00:02:51.725 --> 00:02:52.558
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:52.558 --> 00:02:53.391
- Well that's not all.

00:02:53.391 --> 00:02:55.350
Our season-long partner, Pilot Pen, makers

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.780
of G2, the go-to pen of the
Kelly Clarkson Show, want

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.540
to honor truly unstoppable
people just like y'all.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.970
So they're gonna write
you a check for $1,000.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:06.243
How's that sound?
(audience cheering)

00:03:08.758 --> 00:03:10.200
- That's too cool.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.290
- All right, y'all, have
a blessed afternoon!

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.318
Everybody, before we go,

00:03:15.318 --> 00:03:18.390
the 149th Kentucky Derby airs tomorrow,

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:22.050
Saturday, May 6th and coverage
begins at noon, Eastern.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.850
Check it out on NBC and Peacock.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.440
Thank you to all our guests today,

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.633
Ryan Seacrest, Taylor
Hicks, India Amarteifio,

00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:33.857
Corey Mylchreest, Arsema Thomas and Maya.

00:03:33.857 --> 00:03:34.770
Y'all have a great day,

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:36.987
and if it's not great, try and change it.

